# Product shape

Ctrl UI is an opinionated React + TypeScript design-system kit.

It is not a headless library. It is not a copy-paste catalog. React Aria is an implementation dependency for later composite layers, not the product.

First target consumer: teams building product UI in React who would otherwise compose headless primitives and restyle them. They pick Ctrl UI because WCAG 2.2 AA behavior and a closed visual language ship in the package, and they can theme through semantic tokens without forking.

The kit MUST work in ordinary React. RSC hosts MUST be able to import it without a Next-specific package. Published modules that use client APIs MUST be marked `"use client"`.

A feature consumer MUST be able to install the public (or workspace) package and apply semantic tokens without cloning this repository.

This foundation increment is toolchain + tokens. A consumer-shaped screen is out of validation until a consuming app exists.
